lesson k-in-on-under v=1 format=teach grade=0 unit=6 subject=maths levels=[easy, medium, hard] {
  title "In, on, under, next to"
  goal "Say where something is with in, on, under and next to."

  look {
    scene 29x8 {
      picturecards cards who=["cat", "cat", "cat"] where=["in", "on", "under"] thing=["box", "box", "box"] letters=true at=canvas(1, 1)
    }
    say """
        The cat is in the box, then on the box, then under the box. These words tell us where things
        are: in, on, under, next to, above and below.
      """
  }
  do {
    level easy {
      worked k.where-is-it k=0 level=medium
    }
    practice k.where-is-it count=3 seed=2 easy-count=2
    practice k.which-card-place count=3 seed=3 easy-count=2
    show k.above-below k=0 hard-k=1
    show k.put-it-where
  }
  try stars=2 {
    show k.in-or-on
  }
  try stars=3 {
    show k.follow-the-words k=0 hard-k=1
  }
  remember {
    say "In, on, under, next to: words that say where."
  }

  grown-ups """
    Read each question aloud. The shapes lesson named things; this one is the step on from it,
    saying where they are. The teddy question is for you to watch. If the child mixes in and on,
    play hide and seek with a toy and describe its hiding place together. Off the page, tidy up with
    position words: the book goes on the shelf, the ball goes in the box. Japan, 幼稚園教育要領
    (kindergarten guidelines), 環境, 内容 (8): "日常生活の中で数量や図形などに関心をもつ。" (In daily life,
    take an interest in numbers, amounts and shapes.)
    """
  level easy {
    grown-ups "At this level on the mat is worked in the teacher's pen first, the places are on, in and under, and the cat is above the table."
  }
  level hard {
    grown-ups "At this level the places include next to and by, the cat is below the table, and the three-star needs two clues together."
  }
}
